"A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-c1-04","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"c1-natural","name":"Cambridge English — Bank accounts (C1–C2)","levels":["C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/c1l062-bank-accounts","task":"Tabiiy nutqdagi maqsad va muhim shartlarni tinglab, qisqa xulosa yozing.","lesson":"en-c1-04","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied.","recapQuestions":[{"id":"en-c1-04-recap-0","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Grammatik tanlov va muallif pozitsiyasi: Til vositasini tanlang: Criteria have been ___ twice. (revise)","answers":["revised"],"explanation":"Active agentni, passive jarayon yoki natijani markazga oladi; ikkalasi faktni buzmasligi kerak. Aspect davomiylik, natija va vaqt chegarasini belgilaydi. Grammatik shaklning ritorik ta’sirini dalil bilan izohlang, muallif niyatini taxmin bilan faktga aylantirmang.","hint":"the committee delayed / the decision was delayed / has been reconsidering","options":["revised","revising","revise"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Grammatik tanlov va muallif pozitsiyasi"},{"id":"en-c1-04-recap-1","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Negative adverbialdan keyingi inversion: Til vositasini tanlang: Rarely ___ we seen such agreement.","answers":["have"],"explanation":"Never/rarely/seldom/under no circumstances boshida yordamchi fe’l egadan oldin. Not until bilan inversion asosiy gapda: Not until … did we understand. Inversion rasmiy ta’kid; har gapni bezash uchun qo‘llamang.","hint":"Rarely have … / Not until … did …","options":["have","has","had"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Negative adverbialdan keyingi inversion"},{"id":"en-c1-04-recap-2","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Takrorlash · Cleft va pseudo-cleft: Til vositasini tanlang: It was access ___ concerned them.","answers":["that"],"explanation":"It was X that … fokusni Xga qo‘yadi. What we need is … pseudo-cleft oldingi vaziyatdan yangi talabga o‘tadi. Ta’kid faktning doirasini o‘zgartirmasin; only ishlatilsa eksklyuziv ma’no qo‘shadi.","hint":"It was access that … / What we need is …","options":["that","what","who"],"recap":true,"sourceLesson":"Cleft va pseudo-cleft"}]}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-c1-05','en-c1-05',null,5,5,'published',1,'{"id":"en-c1-05","baseId":"en-c1-05","revision":1,"level":"C1","levelIndex":5,"order":5,"title":"Conditional inversion va ehtiyot chorasi","objective":"Shartni rasmiy yozishmada ma’no saqlangan holda ifodalaysiz.","context":"Conditional inversion va ehtiyot chorasi","prerequisites":["en-c1-04"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for.","Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart.","Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin."],"pattern":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","examples":["Had we known, we would have revised the plan.","Were it not for the grant, the project would stop.","Should you need clarification, please contact us.","Had we not checked, the error would have remained.","Were the timetable clearer, attendance might improve.","Should the trial fail, the original system will remain."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-c1-05-v0","term":"contingency","meaning":"zaxira shart","ipa":"/kənˈtɪndʒənsi/","collocation":"a contingency plan","example":"A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain.” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency."},{"id":"en-c1-05-v1","term":"provision","meaning":"shart bandi","ipa":"/prəˈvɪʒən/","collocation":"a written provision","example":"A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain.” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency."},{"id":"en-c1-05-v2","term":"clarification","meaning":"aniqlashtirish","ipa":"/ˌklærɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","collocation":"seek clarification","example":"Should you need clarification, please contact us."},{"id":"en-c1-05-v3","term":"retain","meaning":"saqlab qolmoq","ipa":"/rɪˈteɪn/","collocation":"retain the original system","example":"retain the original system"}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","Had we known, we would have revised the plan.","Were it not for the grant, the project would stop."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["The proposal needs future contingencies.","The review concerns an unreal past condition.","Separate the two time relations."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"Had we not checked, the error would have remained.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-05-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-c1-05-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: ___ we known, we would have revised it.","answers":["Had"],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["Had","Have","Were"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ we known, we would have revised it.","answers":["Had"],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need"},{"id":"en-c1-05-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["Had we known, we would have revised the plan."],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","tokens":["Had","we","known,","we","would","have","revised","the","plan."]},{"id":"en-c1-05-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Had not we checked, the error would have remained.","answers":["Had we not checked, the error would have remained."],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need"},{"id":"en-c1-05-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["zaxira shart","shart bandi","aniqlashtirish","saqlab qolmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","left":["contingency","provision","clarification","retain"],"options":["zaxira shart","shart bandi","aniqlashtirish","saqlab qolmoq"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Inversion: If we had known, we would have revised the plan.","answers":["Had we known, we would have revised the plan."],"hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for."},{"id":"en-c1-05-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["The proposal needs future contingencies.","The review concerns an unreal past condition.","Separate the two time relations."],"answers":["The proposal needs future contingencies.\nThe review concerns an unreal past condition.\nSeparate the two time relations."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain.” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency. The review also says, “Had we known about the transport problem, we would have revised the timetable.” That clause refers to an unreal past condition. Students initially treat both sentences as future warnings because both begin with an auxiliary. The editor asks them to expand each into an if-clause and identify the time relation. Formal compression is useful only when readers can recover the intended condition. The proposal keeps the future contingency and moves the past reflection to the review section. This separates what the team will do next from what it wishes it had known earlier.","sentences":["A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain.","” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency.","The review also says, “Had we known about the transport problem, we would have revised the timetable.","” That clause refers to an unreal past condition.","Students initially treat both sentences as future warnings because both begin with an auxiliary.","The editor asks them to expand each into an if-clause and identify the time relation.","Formal compression is useful only when readers can recover the intended condition.","The proposal keeps the future contingency and moves the past reflection to the review section.","This separates what the team will do next from what it wishes it had known earlier."],"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-05-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Should the trial fail ma’nosi?","answers":["a future contingency"],"explanation":"Should kelajak ehtimoli.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["a future contingency","a certain failure","an unreal past fact"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Past reflection qayerga ko‘chdi?","answers":["the review section"],"explanation":"Vaqt vazifasi ajratiladi.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["the review section","the contingency list","it was deleted as false"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain.","” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency.","The review also says, “Had we known about the transport problem, we would have revised the timetable.","” That clause refers to an unreal past condition.","Students initially treat both sentences as future warnings because both begin with an auxiliary.","The editor asks them to expand each into an if-clause and identify the time relation.","Formal compression is useful only when readers can recover the intended condition.","The proposal keeps the future contingency and moves the past reflection to the review section.","This separates what the team will do next from what it wishes it had known earlier."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is contingency. A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain. ” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency. Speaker two: My main point is time. Expand the condition to check its time relation. A proposal includes the provision, “Should the trial fail, the original system will remain.” This does not predict failure; it states a contingency. The review also says, “Had we known about the transport problem, we would have revised the timetable.” That clause refers to an unreal past condition. Students initially treat both sentences as future warnings because both begin with an auxiliary. The editor asks them to expand each into an if-clause and identify the time relation. Formal compression is useful only when readers can recover the intended condition. The proposal keeps the future contingency and moves the past reflection to the review section. This separates what the team will do next from what it wishes it had known earlier.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-05.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-05-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Should the trial fail ma’nosi?","answers":["a future contingency"],"explanation":"Should kelajak ehtimoli.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["a future contingency","a certain failure","an unreal past fact"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Past reflection qayerga ko‘chdi?","answers":["the review section"],"explanation":"Vaqt vazifasi ajratiladi.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["the review section","the contingency list","it was deleted as false"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["contingency","time"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["Had we not checked, the error would have remained."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-05-dictation.mp3","transcript":"Had we not checked, the error would have remained."}]},"writing":{"task":"Proposalda ikki kelajak contingency va bitta alohida o‘tmish review yozing.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":420,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"Should the trial fail to improve access, the original timetable will remain in place. Should participants need clarification, the organiser will provide a written explanation before the first session. These provisions describe possible future needs rather than predicting failure. In the review, we acknowledge that, had we known about the transport difficulty earlier, we would have revised the plan. Keeping that reflection separate from the contingency list helps readers distinguish an unreal past condition from a practical commitment for the next stage.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["Had we known, we would have revised the plan.","Were it not for the grant, the project would stop.","Should you need clarification, please contact us."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Proposalda ikki kelajak contingency va bitta alohida o‘tmish review yozing. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":150,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Proposalda ikki kelajak contingency va bitta alohida o‘tmish review yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-c1-05-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ we known, we would have revised it.","answers":["Had"],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need"},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ you need clarification, contact us.","answers":["Should"],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need"},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Were it not ___ the grant, we would stop.","answers":["for"],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need"},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Should the trial fail ma’nosi?","answers":["a future contingency"],"explanation":"Should kelajak ehtimoli.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["a future contingency","a certain failure","an unreal past fact"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Past reflection qayerga ko‘chdi?","answers":["the review section"],"explanation":"Vaqt vazifasi ajratiladi.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["the review section","the contingency list","it was deleted as false"]}],[{"id":"en-c1-05-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Were it not for the grant, the project would stop."],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","tokens":["Were","it","not","for","the","grant,","the","project","would","stop."]},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"___ you need clarification, contact us.","answers":["Should"],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need"},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Had we not checked, the error would have remained."],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","tokens":["Had","we","not","checked,","the","error","would","have","remained."]},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Should the trial fail ma’nosi?","answers":["a future contingency"],"explanation":"Should kelajak ehtimoli.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","options":["a future contingency","a certain failure","an unreal past fact"]},{"id":"en-c1-05-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["Should the trial fail, the original system will remain."],"explanation":"Had we known = if we had known; were it not for = if it were not for. Should you need … kelajak ehtimoli uchun rasmiy shart. Inverted clause yordamchini oldinga oladi, not egadan keyin; vaqt ma’nosi saqlansin.","hint":"Had we known / Were it not for / Should you need","tokens":["Should","the","trial","fail,","the","original","system","will","remain."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"c1-natural","name":"Cambridge English — Bank accounts (C1–C2)","levels":["C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/c1l062-bank-accounts","task":"Tabiiy nutqdagi maqsad va muhim shartlarni tinglab, qisqa xulosa yozing.","lesson":"en-c1-05","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-c1-06','en-c1-06',null,5,6,'published',1,'{"id":"en-c1-06","baseId":"en-c1-06","revision":1,"level":"C1","levelIndex":5,"order":6,"title":"Hedging va epistemic modality","objective":"Da’vo kuchini manba va ehtimolga mos boshqarasiz.","context":"Hedging va epistemic modality","prerequisites":["en-c1-05"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi.","Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring.","Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting."],"pattern":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","examples":["The findings may suggest a trend.","The result appears consistent with our prediction.","The data cannot establish causation.","The response is likely to depend on context.","This explanation must be treated cautiously.","A larger study would be needed to confirm the pattern."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-c1-06-v0","term":"causation","meaning":"sababiy aloqa","ipa":"/kɔːˈzeɪʃən/","collocation":"establish causation","example":"The data cannot establish causation."},{"id":"en-c1-06-v1","term":"correlation","meaning":"birga o‘zgarish","ipa":"/ˌkɒrəˈleɪʃən/","collocation":"observe a correlation","example":"observe a correlation"},{"id":"en-c1-06-v2","term":"plausibility","meaning":"ishonarlilik","ipa":"/ˌplɔːzəˈbɪləti/","collocation":"assess plausibility","example":"assess plausibility"},{"id":"en-c1-06-v3","term":"qualified","meaning":"cheklangan shartli","ipa":"/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪd/","collocation":"a qualified conclusion","example":"A qualified conclusion therefore states the observed change and the uncertainty about its cause separately."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","The findings may suggest a trend.","The result appears consistent with our prediction."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["Confidence increased among participants.","Selection and outside practice were not controlled.","Recommend further investigation with a qualified conclusion."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The response is likely to depend on context.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-06-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-c1-06-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: The findings may ___ a trend. (suggest)","answers":["suggest"],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["suggest","suggests","suggested"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The findings may ___ a trend. (suggest)","answers":["suggest"],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish"},{"id":"en-c1-06-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["The findings may suggest a trend."],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","tokens":["The","findings","may","suggest","a","trend."]},{"id":"en-c1-06-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The correlation proves that the workshop caused improvement.","answers":["The correlation is consistent with improvement, but does not establish causation."],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish"},{"id":"en-c1-06-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["sababiy aloqa","birga o‘zgarish","ishonarlilik","cheklangan shartli"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","left":["causation","correlation","plausibility","qualified"],"options":["sababiy aloqa","birga o‘zgarish","ishonarlilik","cheklangan shartli"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Da’voni cheklang: The workshop caused improvement.","answers":["The findings may suggest that the workshop contributed to improvement."],"hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi."},{"id":"en-c1-06-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["Confidence increased among participants.","Selection and outside practice were not controlled.","Recommend further investigation with a qualified conclusion."],"answers":["Confidence increased among participants.\nSelection and outside practice were not controlled.\nRecommend further investigation with a qualified conclusion."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."},{"id":"en-c1-06-collocations","type":"collocation","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni darsdagi birikmasi bilan moslang.","left":["causation","correlation","plausibility","qualified"],"options":["establish causation","observe a correlation","assess plausibility","a qualified conclusion"],"answers":["establish causation","observe a correlation","assess plausibility","a qualified conclusion"],"hint":"So‘z qaysi birikmada ishlatilishini eslang.","explanation":"Birikmani yozgan gapingizda ham ishlating."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"Students who attended the workshop reported greater confidence afterwards. The report says that the workshop caused the improvement. However, the students volunteered to attend, and no comparison group was observed. The result is consistent with a positive effect, but other explanations remain plausible: motivated students may practise more outside the workshop. A qualified conclusion therefore states the observed change and the uncertainty about its cause separately. This is not excessive caution. It prevents a recommendation from being presented as a demonstrated mechanism. The organiser can still propose another trial, provided the design collects evidence that distinguishes competing explanations. Good modality allows a clear decision while preserving the limits of knowledge.","sentences":["Students who attended the workshop reported greater confidence afterwards.","The report says that the workshop caused the improvement.","However, the students volunteered to attend, and no comparison group was observed.","The result is consistent with a positive effect, but other explanations remain plausible: motivated students may practise more outside the workshop.","A qualified conclusion therefore states the observed change and the uncertainty about its cause separately.","This is not excessive caution.","It prevents a recommendation from being presented as a demonstrated mechanism.","The organiser can still propose another trial, provided the design collects evidence that distinguishes competing explanations.","Good modality allows a clear decision while preserving the limits of knowledge."],"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-06-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Causation nega aniqlanmagan?","answers":["no comparison and self-selection"],"explanation":"Muqobil sabablar bor.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["no comparison and self-selection","confidence never changed","all volunteers are identical"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Hedging qarorni to‘xtatadimi?","answers":["not necessarily"],"explanation":"Sinov tavsiyasi davom etishi mumkin.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["not necessarily","always","it proves the mechanism"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["Students who attended the workshop reported greater confidence afterwards.","The report says that the workshop caused the improvement.","However, the students volunteered to attend, and no comparison group was observed.","The result is consistent with a positive effect, but other explanations remain plausible: motivated students may practise more outside the workshop.","A qualified conclusion therefore states the observed change and the uncertainty about its cause separately.","This is not excessive caution.","It prevents a recommendation from being presented as a demonstrated mechanism.","The organiser can still propose another trial, provided the design collects evidence that distinguishes competing explanations.","Good modality allows a clear decision while preserving the limits of knowledge."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is causation. Students who attended the workshop reported greater confidence afterwards. The report says that the workshop caused the improvement. Speaker two: My main point is uncertainty. Recommend a better trial without claiming that causation has been established. Students who attended the workshop reported greater confidence afterwards. The report says that the workshop caused the improvement. However, the students volunteered to attend, and no comparison group was observed. The result is consistent with a positive effect, but other explanations remain plausible: motivated students may practise more outside the workshop. A qualified conclusion therefore states the observed change and the uncertainty about its cause separately. This is not excessive caution. It prevents a recommendation from being presented as a demonstrated mechanism. The organiser can still propose another trial, provided the design collects evidence that distinguishes competing explanations. Good modality allows a clear decision while preserving the limits of knowledge.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-06.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-06-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Causation nega aniqlanmagan?","answers":["no comparison and self-selection"],"explanation":"Muqobil sabablar bor.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["no comparison and self-selection","confidence never changed","all volunteers are identical"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Hedging qarorni to‘xtatadimi?","answers":["not necessarily"],"explanation":"Sinov tavsiyasi davom etishi mumkin.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["not necessarily","always","it proves the mechanism"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["causation","uncertainty"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The response is likely to depend on context."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-06-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The response is likely to depend on context."}]},"writing":{"task":"Survey sharhini observed change, plausible mechanism va noma’lum qism bilan yozing.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":420,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"Participants reported greater confidence after the workshop. This result is consistent with a positive effect, but the study cannot establish causation because attendance was voluntary and no comparison group was observed. Motivation and additional practice remain plausible explanations. I recommend a further trial that records those factors and compares similar groups. The current evidence supports continued investigation rather than a claim that the mechanism has been demonstrated. Stating that limitation makes the recommendation more precise, not less useful.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["The findings may suggest a trend.","The result appears consistent with our prediction.","The data cannot establish causation."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Survey sharhini observed change, plausible mechanism va noma’lum qism bilan yozing. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":150,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Survey sharhini observed change, plausible mechanism va noma’lum qism bilan yozing.","exit":[[{"id":"en-c1-06-exit0","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The findings may ___ a trend. (suggest)","answers":["suggest"],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish"},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The data cannot ___ causation. (establish)","answers":["establish"],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish"},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit2","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"A study would be ___ to confirm it. (need)","answers":["needed"],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish"},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Causation nega aniqlanmagan?","answers":["no comparison and self-selection"],"explanation":"Muqobil sabablar bor.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["no comparison and self-selection","confidence never changed","all volunteers are identical"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit4","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Hedging qarorni to‘xtatadimi?","answers":["not necessarily"],"explanation":"Sinov tavsiyasi davom etishi mumkin.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["not necessarily","always","it proves the mechanism"]}],[{"id":"en-c1-06-exit-b0","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The result appears consistent with our prediction."],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","tokens":["The","result","appears","consistent","with","our","prediction."]},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit-b1","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The data cannot ___ causation. (establish)","answers":["establish"],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish"},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit-b2","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["The response is likely to depend on context."],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","tokens":["The","response","is","likely","to","depend","on","context."]},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit-b3","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Causation nega aniqlanmagan?","answers":["no comparison and self-selection"],"explanation":"Muqobil sabablar bor.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","options":["no comparison and self-selection","confidence never changed","all volunteers are identical"]},{"id":"en-c1-06-exit-b4","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Gapni tartiblang.","answers":["A larger study would be needed to confirm the pattern."],"explanation":"May suggest, appears consistent with, is likely to turli ehtimol va dalil aloqalarini bildiradi. Must xulosa kuchi; must majburiyat ham bo‘lishi mumkin — kontekstni tekshiring. Hedging noaniqlikni yashirmasin: aynan nima noma’lum va nima aniq ekanini ayting.","hint":"may suggest / appears consistent with / cannot establish","tokens":["A","larger","study","would","be","needed","to","confirm","the","pattern."]}]],"sources":[{"id":"cefr","name":"Council of Europe — CEFR daraja tavsiflari","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"framework","url":"https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages/level-descriptions","task":"Dars maqsadini qila olaman tavsifi bilan solishtiring. PRE — kursning tayyorlov bosqichi.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"pronunciation","name":"Cambridge Dictionary — Pronunciation","levels":["PRE","A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"pronunciation","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/pronunciation/","task":"Darsdan ikki so‘z tanlang, UK/US talaffuzini eshiting va urg‘uni qayd eting.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-grammar","name":"British Council — Grammar","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"grammar","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar","task":"Darajangizdagi dars mavzusini toping va bitta o‘xshash misol yozing.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-read","name":"British Council — Reading","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"reading","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/reading","task":"O‘z darajangizdagi matnni tanlang; asosiy fikr va bitta dalilni ajrating.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-write","name":"British Council — Writing","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"writing","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/writing","task":"Darajangizdagi namunaning kirish, asosiy qism va yakunini tahlil qiling.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"bc-listen","name":"British Council — Listening (A1–C1)","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/listening","task":"Mos daraja audiosini transkriptsiz tinglang; keyin yozuv bilan tekshiring.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"cambridge","name":"Cambridge English — Activities","levels":["A1","A2","B1","B2","C1"],"skill":"integrated","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/","task":"A1–A2, B1–B2 yoki C1–C2 filtrini qo‘llang; dars ko‘nikmasiga mos mashqni tanlang.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."},{"id":"c1-natural","name":"Cambridge English — Bank accounts (C1–C2)","levels":["C1"],"skill":"listening","url":"https://www.cambridgeenglish.org/learning-english/activities-for-learners/c1l062-bank-accounts","task":"Tabiiy nutqdagi maqsad va muhim shartlarni tinglab, qisqa xulosa yozing.","lesson":"en-c1-06","verified":"2026-10-05","mode":"link","rights":"Manba saytida bajariladi; himoyalangan matn yoki audio ko‘chirilmagan."}],"recapEvery":4,"project":false,"rights":"Original SinfQuiz content; local Flite synthetic speech. Educational references are linked, not copied."}'::jsonb) on conflict(id,revision) do nothing;
insert into public.sq_en_content(id,base_id,owner_id,level,ordinal,status,revision,payload) values('en-c1-07','en-c1-07',null,5,7,'published',1,'{"id":"en-c1-07","baseId":"en-c1-07","revision":1,"level":"C1","levelIndex":5,"order":7,"title":"Murakkab reporting va passive","objective":"Vaqt, manba va dalil kuchini bitta attributionda saqlaysiz.","context":"Murakkab reporting va passive","prerequisites":["en-c1-06"],"minutes":55,"skills":["grammar","vocabulary","pronunciation","listening","reading","writing","speaking"],"rules":["Is believed to have been changed oldingi passive hodisaga ishora qiladi.","It has been suggested that … taklif, established fact emas.","Bir manbani ko‘p sayt takrorlashi mustaqil tasdiq bo‘lmaydi."],"pattern":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","examples":["The policy is believed to have been revised.","It has been suggested that access improved.","The report is understood to be preliminary.","The figures are said to have been checked.","The claim has not been independently confirmed.","The original source should be identified."],"vocabulary":[{"id":"en-c1-07-v0","term":"independent","meaning":"mustaqil","ipa":"/ˌɪndɪˈpendənt/","collocation":"independent confirmation","example":"The claim has not been independently confirmed."},{"id":"en-c1-07-v1","term":"preliminary","meaning":"dastlabki","ipa":"/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri/","collocation":"a preliminary report","example":"The report is understood to be preliminary."},{"id":"en-c1-07-v2","term":"circulate","meaning":"tarqalmoq","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkjəleɪt/","collocation":"circulate a claim","example":"circulate a claim"},{"id":"en-c1-07-v3","term":"trace","meaning":"izini topmoq","ipa":"/treɪs/","collocation":"trace a source","example":"The student researcher traces every post to the same preliminary report."}],"visuals":[{"kind":"argument","title":"Ma’no va tuzilish","items":["is believed to have been / has been suggested that","The policy is believed to have been revised.","It has been suggested that access improved."]},{"kind":"argument","title":"Fikr va dalilning aloqasi","items":["The claim appears in several posts.","All posts trace to one preliminary proposal.","Repeated attribution is not independent confirmation."]}],"pronunciation":{"focus":"Gapdagi mazmunli so‘zlarni urg‘u bilan ayting. Nuqtada to‘xtab, yozuvni qayta tinglang.","text":"The figures are said to have been checked.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-07-dictation.mp3"},"exercises":[{"id":"en-c1-07-choice","type":"choice","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Til vositasini tanlang: The policy is believed to have been ___. (revise)","answers":["revised"],"explanation":"Is believed to have been changed oldingi passive hodisaga ishora qiladi. It has been suggested that … taklif, established fact emas. Bir manbani ko‘p sayt takrorlashi mustaqil tasdiq bo‘lmaydi.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","options":["revised","revising","revise"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-gap","type":"grammarFill","skill":"grammar","prompt":"The policy is believed to have been ___. (revise)","answers":["revised"],"explanation":"Is believed to have been changed oldingi passive hodisaga ishora qiladi. It has been suggested that … taklif, established fact emas. Bir manbani ko‘p sayt takrorlashi mustaqil tasdiq bo‘lmaydi.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that"},{"id":"en-c1-07-order","type":"order","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Kartalarni to‘g‘ri tartibga qo‘ying.","answers":["The policy is believed to have been revised."],"explanation":"Is believed to have been changed oldingi passive hodisaga ishora qiladi. It has been suggested that … taklif, established fact emas. Bir manbani ko‘p sayt takrorlashi mustaqil tasdiq bo‘lmaydi.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","tokens":["The","policy","is","believed","to","have","been","revised."]},{"id":"en-c1-07-fix","type":"correction","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Several copies of one report provide independent confirmation.","answers":["Several copies of one report do not provide independent confirmation."],"explanation":"Is believed to have been changed oldingi passive hodisaga ishora qiladi. It has been suggested that … taklif, established fact emas. Bir manbani ko‘p sayt takrorlashi mustaqil tasdiq bo‘lmaydi.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that"},{"id":"en-c1-07-vocabulary","type":"matching","skill":"vocabulary","prompt":"So‘zlarni ma’nolari bilan moslang.","answers":["mustaqil","dastlabki","tarqalmoq","izini topmoq"],"explanation":"So‘zni alohida emas, darsdagi birikma va gap bilan eslang.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","left":["independent","preliminary","circulate","trace"],"options":["mustaqil","dastlabki","tarqalmoq","izini topmoq"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-transform","type":"transformation","skill":"grammar","prompt":"Oldingi passive reporting: People believe someone revised the policy.","answers":["The policy is believed to have been revised."],"hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","explanation":"Is believed to have been changed oldingi passive hodisaga ishora qiladi."},{"id":"en-c1-07-paragraphs","type":"paragraphOrder","skill":"reading","prompt":"Fikrni tartiblang: da’vo → dalil → talqin.","tokens":["The claim appears in several posts.","All posts trace to one preliminary proposal.","Repeated attribution is not independent confirmation."],"answers":["The claim appears in several posts.\nAll posts trace to one preliminary proposal.\nRepeated attribution is not independent confirmation."],"hint":"Da’vo nimani aytadi? Dalil nimani ko‘rsatadi?","explanation":"Dalil yakuniy xulosaning o‘rnini bosmaydi; talqin ularning aloqasini tushuntiradi."}],"reading":{"title":"Asosiy matn va muallif pozitsiyasi","text":"Several posts state that the access policy is believed to have been revised. The wording sounds cautious, yet none identifies who believes it or what revision occurred. The student researcher traces every post to the same preliminary report. Repetition has created an appearance of confirmation without adding an independent source. The original report says only that a revision was proposed. The researcher rewrites the summary to name the report and distinguish proposal from implementation. Complex reporting forms can preserve useful time relations, but they can also conceal missing attribution. A reliable analysis asks who made the claim, which event is described, and whether the source supports the stronger version now circulating.","sentences":["Several posts state that the access policy is believed to have been revised.","The wording sounds cautious, yet none identifies who believes it or what revision occurred.","The student researcher traces every post to the same preliminary report.","Repetition has created an appearance of confirmation without adding an independent source.","The original report says only that a revision was proposed.","The researcher rewrites the summary to name the report and distinguish proposal from implementation.","Complex reporting forms can preserve useful time relations, but they can also conceal missing attribution.","A reliable analysis asks who made the claim, which event is described, and whether the source supports the stronger version now circulating."],"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-07-reading0","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Ko‘p posts nega tasdiq emas?","answers":["they repeat one preliminary source"],"explanation":"Mustaqil dalil qo‘shilmagan.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","options":["they repeat one preliminary source","they use different fonts","all proposals are implemented"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-reading1","type":"choice","skill":"reading","prompt":"Original report nima dedi?","answers":["a revision was proposed"],"explanation":"Proposal amalga oshirish emas.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","options":["a revision was proposed","a revision was completed","the policy never existed"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-evidence","type":"evidence","skill":"reading","prompt":"Vaziyatni tanishtiradigan birinchi jumlani tanlang.","answers":["0"],"explanation":"Birinchi jumla matn vaziyatini tanishtiradi; keyingi jumlalar uni rivojlantiradi.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","options":["Several posts state that the access policy is believed to have been revised.","The wording sounds cautious, yet none identifies who believes it or what revision occurred.","The student researcher traces every post to the same preliminary report.","Repetition has created an appearance of confirmation without adding an independent source.","The original report says only that a revision was proposed.","The researcher rewrites the summary to name the report and distinguish proposal from implementation.","Complex reporting forms can preserve useful time relations, but they can also conceal missing attribution.","A reliable analysis asks who made the claim, which event is described, and whether the source supports the stronger version now circulating."]}]},"listening":{"title":"Boshqa nuqtayi nazarni tinglang","transcript":"Speaker one: Our key word is source. Several posts state that the access policy is believed to have been revised. The wording sounds cautious, yet none identifies who believes it or what revision occurred. Speaker two: My main point is independence. Trace the original source before treating repeated reports as confirmation. Several posts state that the access policy is believed to have been revised. The wording sounds cautious, yet none identifies who believes it or what revision occurred. The student researcher traces every post to the same preliminary report. Repetition has created an appearance of confirmation without adding an independent source. The original report says only that a revision was proposed. The researcher rewrites the summary to name the report and distinguish proposal from implementation. Complex reporting forms can preserve useful time relations, but they can also conceal missing attribution. A reliable analysis asks who made the claim, which event is described, and whether the source supports the stronger version now circulating.","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-07.mp3","synthetic":true,"questions":[{"id":"en-c1-07-listening0","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Ko‘p posts nega tasdiq emas?","answers":["they repeat one preliminary source"],"explanation":"Mustaqil dalil qo‘shilmagan.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","options":["they repeat one preliminary source","they use different fonts","all proposals are implemented"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-listening1","type":"choice","skill":"listening","prompt":"Original report nima dedi?","answers":["a revision was proposed"],"explanation":"Proposal amalga oshirish emas.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","options":["a revision was proposed","a revision was completed","the policy never existed"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-audio-table","type":"table","skill":"listening","prompt":"Tinglangan ma’lumotni jadvalga yozing.","answers":["source","independence"],"explanation":"Jadvaldagi javoblar yozuvda aynan aytilgan. Mavjud bo‘lmagan tafsilotni taxmin qilmang.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","rows":["Birinchi gapdagi asosiy so‘z","Sherikning asosiy fikri"]},{"id":"en-c1-07-dictation","type":"dictation","skill":"listening","prompt":"Eshitgan gapingizni yozing.","answers":["The figures are said to have been checked."],"explanation":"Gapdagi asosiy so‘zlar, yordamchi fe’l va inkor saqlanishi kerak.","hint":"is believed to have been / has been suggested that","audio":"/english-course/v7.23/en-c1-07-dictation.mp3","transcript":"The figures are said to have been checked."}]},"writing":{"task":"Source audit yozing: attribution, time relation va claimning kuchaygan joyi.","audience":"Maktab kengashi yoki loyiha guruhi","minWords":70,"maxWords":420,"plan":["Da’vo va maqsadni aniqlang.","Reading va listeningdan bir dalilni qiyoslang.","Cheklov yoki qarshi fikrni tushuntiring.","Auditoriyaga mos amaliy xulosa yozing."],"model":"The circulating posts all derive from one preliminary report. That report proposed a revision; it did not confirm implementation. The policy is therefore not known to have been revised. Repetition across several pages should not be counted as independent confirmation. Our summary should name the original source and preserve its status as a proposal. Complex reporting language is useful when it clarifies attribution and time, but the wording should not make unsupported information appear more established than it is.","modelNotes":["Kirishda auditoriya va maqsad aniq.","Asosiy qism dalilni talqin bilan bog‘laydi.","Yakun haddan tashqari umumlashtirmaydi."],"phrases":["The policy is believed to have been revised.","It has been suggested that access improved.","The report is understood to be preliminary."],"checklist":["Topshiriq va auditoriyaga mos yozdim.","Fikrni o‘z so‘zlarim bilan ifodaladim.","Darsdagi shaklni to‘g‘ri ishlatdim.","Imlo, bog‘lanish va tinish belgilarini tekshirdim."]},"speaking":{"task":"Reading va listeningni taqqoslang. Source audit yozing: attribution, time relation va claimning kuchaygan joyi. Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","seconds":150,"prompts":["Reading va listening qayerda mos, qayerda farqli?","Sherigingizning e’tiroziga javob bering.","Qaysi dalil xulosangizni o‘zgartirishi mumkin?"],"rubric":["Vazifani bajarish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Bog‘langan, tushunarli nutq","Talaffuz va muloqot"]},"rubrics":{"writing":["Mazmun va vazifani bajarish","Tuzilish va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va uslub","Grammatika va imlo"],"speaking":["Vazifa va o‘zaro muloqot","Ravonlik va bog‘lanish","Til vositalari va aniqlik","Tushunarlilik va talaffuz"]},"realTask":"Source audit yozing: attribution, time relation va claimning kuchaygan joyi.","exit":[[{"id":"en-c1-07-exit0","type"